{"ts": "2026-10-15T04:45:00Z", "by": "model:muse-spark", "entity": "type", "id": "BM.X.10-cents", "op": "set", "field": "description", "old": "", "new": "The obverse bears the crowned portrait of Queen Elizabeth II facing right, engraved by Raphael Maklouf. The reverse shows the Bermuda lily, the island's floral emblem, engraved by Michael Rizzello, with the date above and TEN CENTS below. Bermuda adopted its decimal dollar on 6 February 1970, and the lily has anchored the 10-cent reverse ever since.", "source": "NGC: Bermuda 10 Cents KM 46 - Obverse: Crowned head right (Raphael Maklouf); Reverse: Bermuda lily (Michael Rizzello) (https://www.ngccoin.com/price-guide/world/bermuda-10-cents-km-46-1986-1998-cuid-1043993-duid-1290485); decimalisation 6 Feb 1970 (https://currencies.fandom.com/wiki/Bermudian_1_cent_coin)", "verified": false, "phase": 2, "confidence": "med", "provenance": {"model": "muse-spark", "prompt_version": "DESCRIPTIONS@2026-10-15", "workflow": "phase2-research", "inputs": [{"file": "collection design records + web research (see source URLs)"}], "run_id": "type-descriptions-20261015"}}
