{"ts": "2026-10-15T04:45:00Z", "by": "model:muse-spark", "entity": "type", "id": "CL.KM.219.2", "op": "set", "field": "description", "old": "", "new": "The obverse shows the profile of Bernardo O'Higgins, liberator of Chile, with REPUBLICA DE CHILE and LIBERTADOR B. O'HIGGINS around the portrait and the Santiago (So) mint mark. The reverse carries the large value 50 with PESOS and the date inside a laurel wreath. The decagonal aluminum-bronze 50 pesos, engraved by Rene Thenot, has been a workhorse of Chilean circulation since 1981.", "source": "NGC: Chile 50 Pesos KM 219.2 (https://www.ngccoin.com/price-guide/world/chile-50-pesos-km-219.2-1988-2013-cuid-1039037-duid-1281684); design details - O'Higgins profile, LIBERTADOR B. O'HIGGINS, decagonal, laurel branches, designer Rene Thenot (https://www.lastdodo.com/en/items/6074529-chile-50-pesos-2011); Banco Central de Chile via (https://pepeschile.com/pesos/50pesos/)", "verified": false, "phase": 2, "confidence": "med", "provenance": {"model": "muse-spark", "prompt_version": "DESCRIPTIONS@2026-10-15", "workflow": "phase2-research", "inputs": [{"file": "collection design records + web research (see source URLs)"}], "run_id": "type-descriptions-20261015"}}
{"ts": "2026-10-15T04:45:00Z", "by": "model:muse-spark", "entity": "type", "id": "CO.KM.295", "op": "set", "field": "description", "old": "", "new": "The reverse shows the spectacled (Andean) bear, Tremarctos ornatus, with its common and scientific names - one of three flagship species of Colombian biodiversity chosen for the new coin family. The obverse carries the large 50 with PESOS, REPUBLICA DE COLOMBIA and the date over a wavy field evoking moving water. Issued from 2012, the series was designed by Jose Antonio Suarez (the 50 and 200 pesos) and Johana Calle (the 100), and won the IACA award for best new circulating series.", "source": "Banco de la Republica: spectacled bear one of three biodiversity species on the new COP$50/100/200 family, designs by Jose Antonio Suarez and Johana Calle, circulating from H2 2012 (https://banrep.gov.co/en/print/pdf/node/32360); NGC: Colombia 50 Pesos KM 295 - Reverse: Spectacled bear (Tremarctos ornatus) (https://www.ngccoin.com/price-guide/world/colombia-50-pesos-km-295-2012-2015-cuid-1064894-duid-1307603)", "verified": false, "phase": 2, "confidence": "med", "provenance": {"model": "muse-spark", "prompt_version": "DESCRIPTIONS@2026-10-15", "workflow": "phase2-research", "inputs": [{"file": "collection design records + web research (see source URLs)"}], "run_id": "type-descriptions-20261015"}}
{"ts": "2026-10-15T04:45:00Z", "by": "model:muse-spark", "entity": "type", "id": "CR.KM.214.2", "op": "set", "field": "description", "old": "", "new": "The obverse sets Costa Rica's national arms inside a heptagon - the seven-sided frame stands for the seven provinces - with a large sailing ship and AMERICA CENTRAL. The reverse reads 5 COLONES with the B.C.C.R. (Banco Central de Costa Rica) initials, flanked by coffee branches and Braille dots for the visually impaired. Coffee dominated Costa Rica's exports for over a century, and the heptagon-framed arms make this one of the most distinctive Latin American designs.", "source": "LastDodo: Costa Rica 5 colones 1985 = KM# 214.2 (https://www.lastdodo.com/en/areas/628741-5-colones); design elements (heptagon arms, ship, coffee branches, Braille) per collection design record CR.KM.214.2; BCCR coinage conventions (crossed coffee branches, B.C.C.R. initials) per Banco Central de Costa Rica contract history (https://worldnumismatics.com/wp/wp-content/uploads/2017/11/MCC-Newsletter-Nov2017-Final-Web.pdf)", "verified": false, "phase": 2, "confidence": "med", "provenance": {"model": "muse-spark", "prompt_version": "DESCRIPTIONS@2026-10-15", "workflow": "phase2-research", "inputs": [{"file": "collection design records + web research (see source URLs)"}], "run_id": "type-descriptions-20261015"}}
{"ts": "2026-10-15T04:45:00Z", "by": "model:muse-spark", "entity": "type", "id": "FR.KM.888b.1", "op": "set", "field": "description", "old": "", "new": "The obverse shows a laureate head of Marianne facing left, engraved by Andre-Henri Lavrillier, embodying the French Republic. The reverse reads RF above 5 FRANCS and the date within a sectioned laurel wreath. Struck in aluminum for the post-war Provisional Government (1944-1947), this lightweight 3.5-gram emergency issue circulated while France rebuilt its coinage after 1945.", "source": "NGC: France 5 Francs KM 888b.1 - aluminum, laureate head left, denomination above date within sectioned wreath (https://www.ngccoin.com/price-guide/world/france-5-francs-km-888b.1-1945-1952-cuid-1127884-duid-1263715); engraver Andre-Henri Lavrillier (1885-1958), Provisional Government 1944-1947 (https://www.numisaisne.fr/en/coins/20699-france-km-888-5-francs-1946-c-castelsarrasin-type-lavrillier-f.html)", "verified": false, "phase": 2, "confidence": "med", "provenance": {"model": "muse-spark", "prompt_version": "DESCRIPTIONS@2026-10-15", "workflow": "phase2-research", "inputs": [{"file": "collection design records + web research (see source URLs)"}], "run_id": "type-descriptions-20261015"}}
{"ts": "2026-10-15T04:45:00Z", "by": "model:muse-spark", "entity": "type", "id": "GT.KM.239.2", "op": "set", "field": "description", "old": "", "new": "The obverse carries Guatemala's national arms - crossed rifles and swords behind a liberty cap over a scroll - with LIBERTAD 15 DE SEPTIEMBRE DE 1821 and the 0.720 silver fineness. The reverse shows the resplendent quetzal, the national bird that gives the currency its name, perched on an engraved pillar with LEY DE 26 DE NOVIEMBRE DE 1924. Struck in .720 fine silver, this type belongs to the classic 1925-1949 quetzal coinage.", "source": "NGC: Guatemala 10 Centavos KM 239.1 - silver 0.720, obverse national arms, reverse bird on engraved pillar (https://www.ngccoin.com/price-guide/world/guatemala-10-centavos-km-239.1-1925-1949-cuid-1200558-duid-1332992); quetzal-on-pillar reverse and 1924 law per collection design record GT.KM.239.2", "verified": false, "phase": 2, "confidence": "med", "provenance": {"model": "muse-spark", "prompt_version": "DESCRIPTIONS@2026-10-15", "workflow": "phase2-research", "inputs": [{"file": "collection design records + web research (see source URLs)"}], "run_id": "type-descriptions-20261015"}}
